speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I move:
That, notwithstanding any Standing Order of this House, the chairman of any legislative committee shall be empowered to call a meeting for the purposes of organization, pursuant to Standing Order 113(3), at his or her discretion but, in any case, shall do so no later than lO sitting days after this House resumes sitting in September, 1989;
Provided that this Order does not apply to the legislative committee on Bill C-21.

I am informed by the Departments of Finance and Supply and Services as follows:
a)	Budget in Brief: 1984-400,500; 1985-707,000;
1986-355,750;	1987-200,000;	1988-291,000;
1989-460,000
b)	Other standard budget documents: 1984-64,500;
1984 (Economic Statement)-50,600; 1985-64,500; 1986-80,750;	1987-95,000;	1988-91,000;
1989-110,000
i)	Because of Budget secrecy requirements, a wide variety of security measures exist. These include ensuring that personnel who are required to work on the preparation, production and distribution of the Budget have undergone an appropriate security screening; and that the locations where Budget materials are handled, including the printing, distribution and waste storage areas, are in a secure environment.
ii)	In accordance with government security policy, all classified Budget "surplus material", including copies that are rejected due to printing process errors, is baled under guard and then held in a secure area until after the Budget is tabled (released). At that time, the now unclassified "surplus material" is turned over to a private sector waste paper disposal firm under contract with the government.

Mr. Speaker, there have been discussions among the Parties. I think you will find unanimous consent from me to put the following motion immediately, and for it to be voted on without debate. I move:
That, pursuant to Section 56 of the Canadian Security Intelligence Services Act and Section 7 of the Security Offences Act,
That, a special committee of the House of Commons be appointed to be the committee to undertake a comprehensive review of the provisions and operation of the Canadian Security Intelligence Service Act with a committee empowered to meet after July 16, 1989, and with the committee to report no later than July 16, 1990; and
That, the committee have all the powers of a Standing Committee and;
That, the membership of the said special committee to be as follows;
Mr. Thacker, (chairman), and Messrs, Brewin, Homer, Lee, Littlechild, Nunziata, Tremblay (Lotbiniere), Tetreault.
